# Raw tensor kernels may hold overflow, but every language scalar read crosses
# num_guard in both strict modes. Finite values and bounds remain unchanged.
b is buffer of 4
b[0] is 1e300
b[1] is 1e300
b[2] is 1e300
b[3] is 1e300
m is reshape of [b, 2, 2]
p is matmul of [m, m]
print of (p[0] > 1e308)
print of p[0]
f is buffer of 1
f[0] is 14.5
q is reshape of [f, 1, 1]
print of q[0]
try:
    print of q[1]
catch e:
    print of e.kind
